Schema disclosure: Workflow tool_input shape is SCHEMA-DOC-DERIVED (R5), not captured live -- in particular, the existence of a scriptPath-only (file-reference) invocation shape, alongside an inline-script shape, is inferred from the dispatch task description, not observed.

Disclosed boundary: this guard only inspects INLINE scripts (tool_input.script). A scriptPath-only or name-only invocation (no tool_input.script key at all) has no inline text for the guard to scan for agent( calls, so it fails OPEN (allow) rather than denying or erroring. This is a known, deliberate coverage gap, not a bug -- a scriptPath-referenced file's model-pin discipline is out of scope for this hook. Expected result: allow (non-deny stdout, same contract as cases b/c).
